	'about_h1' => 'About the College',
	'about_lead' => 'Yubi College is a small independent college in Esterhaven training working adults to interpret between spoken language and sign language. Founded in 1996, we combine weekday evening study and Saturday setting practice led by Deaf tutors.',
	'about_s1_h' => 'Our history: from a public library in 1996',
	'about_s1_p' => 'Yubi College was founded in 1996 by Johanna Reiss, a Deaf teacher, and Tobias Mendel, a hospital interpreter. They began with a Saturday class of eleven adults in the meeting room of the Calloway Street public library in Esterhaven. Both founders recognized that deaf people were routinely attending medical appointments, courtroom hearings, and parent-teacher consultations without qualified interpreters. Working people who wished to retrain had nowhere to study without quitting their jobs. Over three decades, that initial Saturday gathering expanded into an established independent college, maintaining its founding commitment to small cohorts, working adult learners, and direct community service.',
