	'letters_h' => 'Term letters',
	'letters_p' => 'Three letters a year, in January, April and August: taster-evening dates, a note from the table, and when applications open. Nothing else, and you can leave any time.',
	'logo_name' => 'Yubi College',
	'logo_sub' => 'Sign-language interpreter training',
	'newsletter_h1' => 'Term Letters',
	'newsletter_lead' => 'Our term letters provide quiet, infrequent updates from 3 Weaver’s Yard for prospective students and supporters. We send exactly three letters each year to keep you informed about key dates and teaching practice.',
	'newsletter_s1_h' => 'What do the term letters include and when are they sent?',
	'newsletter_s1_p' => 'We publish our term letters three times a year, arriving in January, April, and August. Each letter is written directly by our teaching faculty and contains only essential college news: upcoming taster-evening dates, notification of when course applications open, and a short reflective note from the Saturday table sharing real interpreting challenges discussed by our students and tutors. We do not send marketing promotions, third-party announcements, or frequent bulletins. The letters exist simply to offer an honest glimpse into our training community and keep prospective adult learners informed of relevant admissions deadlines.',
	'newsletter_s1_sub' => '01 · What is in them',
	'newsletter_s2_h' => 'How do we handle your privacy and how can you unsubscribe?',
	'newsletter_s2_p' => 'Your privacy is treated with complete respect. We collect your email address solely to deliver the three seasonal term letters and will never sell, lease, or share your contact information with external bodies or advertisers. If you no longer wish to receive our letters, you can leave the list at any time by clicking the unsubscribe link included at the bottom of every email, or by sending a brief request to hello@yubicollege.example. Once requested, your address is removed immediately from our database with no questions asked and no follow-up correspondence.',
	'newsletter_s2_sub' => '02 · Privacy',
	'newsletter_sub' => 'Three letters a year',
	'nf_b' => 'Back to the home page',
	'nf_eyebrow' => '404',
	'nf_h' => 'This page is not here',
	'nf_p' => 'The page may have moved. Start again from the home page, or look at the courses.',
	'nl_h' => 'Term letters',
	'nl_p' => 'January, April and August: taster-evening dates, a note from the table, and when applications open. We use your address only for these letters, and every letter says how to leave.',
	'nl_sub' => 'Three letters a year',
	'notices_h' => 'Notices',
	'notices_link' => 'All notices →',
	'notices_sub' => 'News from Weaver’s Yard',
	'placements_h1' => 'Placements',
	'placements_lead' => 'During the second year of the Interpreter Diploma, every student undertakes 60 hours of supervised placement across Esterhaven. You shadow working professionals across our eleven partner settings to observe real public service interpreting firsthand.',
	'placements_s1_h' => 'How do the 60 placement hours work?',
	'placements_s1_p' => 'In year two of the Interpreter Diploma, students complete 60 placement hours divided equally across three distinct sectors: 20 hours in a hospital or clinic, 20 hours in a court or tribunal, and 20 hours in a school. Placements consist of direct shadowing alongside an experienced, registered interpreter. After each session, the supervising interpreter reviews your observations and signs your official practice log. Our placements coordinator, Clara Moreau, oversees every placement allocation and conducts an in-person site visit to each student at least once per setting, ensuring clinical safety, professional boundaries, and supportive educational mentoring.',
	'placements_s1_sub' => '01 · How it works',
	'placements_s2_h' => 'Healthcare placements: hospitals and clinical services',
	'placements_s2_p' => 'Our healthcare placements encompass four hospitals and clinics across Esterhaven, including outpatient departments at Esterhaven General Hospital and pediatric services at Northgate Children’s Hospital. Students shadow registered practitioners through routine outpatient consultations, pre-operative assessments, physiotherapy sessions, and audiology appointments. By standing beside seasoned professionals in real clinical rooms, students observe how medical terminology is conveyed accurately under pressure, how doctors and Deaf patients negotiate communication barriers, and how interpreters position themselves physically to maintain clear sightlines while respecting clinical sterility and patient privacy.',
	'placements_s2_sub' => '02 · In a hospital',
	'placements_s3_h' => 'Legal placements: courts and tribunals',
	'placements_s3_p' => 'The college partners with three legal institutions in the city, including Esterhaven Magistrates’ Court and Quayside Family Court. During their 20 legal placement hours, students observe judicial hearings, bail applications, civil dispute tribunals, and preparatory client conferences. Shadowing court interpreters provides essential insight into legal formality, the administration of witness oaths, and the delivery of statutory warnings. Students see firsthand how interpreters maintain absolute impartiality, navigate rapid evidentiary exchanges, and preserve procedural justice without intervening in the proceedings or altering the formal legal register.',
	'placements_s3_sub' => '03 · In a court',
	'placements_s4_h' => 'Educational placements: schools and deaf units',
	'placements_s4_p' => 'We work with four partner schools across the city, including Harrow Field Primary and the dedicated deaf unit at Linden Bank School. Educational placements expose students to primary classrooms, secondary subject lessons, school assemblies, and parent-teacher consultations. Trainees observe how educational interpreters adapt signing register to the developmental age of the child, collaborate with classroom teachers, and support learning without fostering unhealthy dependence. These 20 hours demonstrate how sign language interpretation operates as an empowering tool for educational inclusion within standard academic environments.',
	'placements_s4_sub' => '04 · In a school',
	'placements_s5_h' => 'What will you not do on placement?',
	'placements_s5_p' => 'Our placement policy is clear and non-negotiable: you will never interpret alone on placement. Yubi College students attend clinical, judicial, and educational environments strictly in a shadowing capacity under the direct oversight of a qualified, registered professional. Trainees are not substitute staff and are never permitted to take responsibility for solo assignments, emergency calls, or unsupervised client consultations. This absolute boundary protects vulnerable Deaf service users, upholds public service standards, and ensures that student learning remains reflective, safe, and free from inappropriate institutional liability.',
	'placements_s5_sub' => '05 · The one rule',
	'placements_sub' => 'Sixty hours, eleven settings',
	'priv1_h' => 'Who we are',
	'priv1_p' => 'Yubi College is a small independent college at 3 Weaver’s Yard, Calloway Street, Esterhaven. You can reach us at hello@yubicollege.example or on +00 41 555 0187. This page says what we keep when you write to us, book a taster evening or ask for the term letters.',
	'priv2_h' => 'What we keep and why',
	'priv2_p' => 'When you send a booking or a question, we keep your name, your address, how you want us to reply and what you wrote, so that Yara Lindqvist can answer. If you ask for the term letters we keep your email address for that purpose only. We do not sell or share your details, and we do not use them for anything else.',
	'priv3_h' => 'How long, and your choices',
	'priv3_p' => 'Booking and enquiry messages are deleted twelve months after the last reply, unless you apply, in which case they become part of your application file. Every term letter says how to leave. You can ask us at any time to show you what we hold, correct it or delete it; write to the address above and we will answer within ten working days.',
	'priv4_h' => 'This website',
	'priv4_p' => 'This site does not set advertising or tracking cookies. If we add a service that does, we will say so here first and ask you before it runs.',
	'privacy_h1' => 'Privacy',
	'privacy_lead' => 'A plain account of what Yubi College keeps when you get in touch, and what you can ask us to do with it.',
	'privacy_sub' => 'How we handle your details',
	'room_l' => 'SATURDAY · 11:20',
	'room_p' => 'Eighteen people, nine pairs. One signs as a Deaf witness, one interprets for an invented magistrate, and Elias walks between the tables listening. Nobody is graded today. The point is to make the mistake here, not in a courtroom.',
